  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SheSTEM: Career Knows No Gender</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh needs more women in science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (STEM): industry practitioners, teachers, agricultural leaders, scientists, mathemati cians, and engineers among others as industries evolve. SheSTEM: a multi-year, consortium-driven program aims to serve as a nexus between public university students and public (primarily) &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; private businesses to increase skills, engagement, participation, eq uity, and inclusion in STEM careers. The project takes a two-pronged approach. On the one hand, it equips the women students with in-demand advanced business- and critical-thinking skills combined with their STEM knowledge, to ensure a successful transition to both public and private organizations; on the other hand, the project actively promotes gender-inclusive public recruitment strategies, sensitizing and advocating for greater representation of women in STEM employment nationwide. By integrating these efforts, SheSTEM aims to expedite the process of women&#x2019;s empowerment in STEM fields, driving meaningful progress an</narrative>
  </description>
